{
 "_about": "Footprint-name \u2192 JLCPCB CPL rotation/offset corrections. KiCad footprints use IPC-7351 zero orientation (pin 1 top-left), JLC's assembly library mostly uses the reel (EIA-481) orientation, so some packages need a fixed rotation added before upload. Patterns are Python regexes matched (re.search) against the footprint name without its library prefix; the first match wins. Values are the community-maintained JLC correction facts (the cpl_rotations_db that Bouni's kicad-jlcpcb-tools downloads from matthewlai/JLCKicadTools), re-expressed as data. Per-part overrides: put a 'JLC Rotation Offset' (degrees) and/or 'JLC Position Offset' ('x,y' mm) field on the symbol/footprint, or add rules to <project>/.copper/jlc_rotations.json (same format; project rules are tried first). Always confirm orientation in JLC's 3D/CPL preview.",
 "bottom_side": "rotation_bottom = (180 - kicad_rotation) % 360, then + correction (same convention as kicad-jlcpcb-tools)",
